SUBTASK 6.2: src/util/id.rs contains several unnamed magic numbers in the ID generation algorithm that controls collision avoidance:

Line 133: for _ in 0..10 — nonce retry count per hash length
  Add: const NONCE_RETRIES_PER_LENGTH: u32 = 10;

Line 150: 12 — fallback hash length when max_hash_length exhausted
  Add: const FALLBACK_HASH_LENGTH: usize = 12;

Line 161: 1000 — safety break threshold for desperate ID generation
  Add: const SAFETY_BREAK_THRESHOLD: u32 = 1000;

Line 169: 2000 — hard stop to prevent infinite loop
  Add: const HARD_STOP_LIMIT: u32 = 2000;

Line 520: 6 — abbreviation threshold for prefix length
  Add: const ABBREVIATION_THRESHOLD: usize = 6;

Line 543: 3 — fallback abbreviation length
  Add: const FALLBACK_ABBREVIATION_LENGTH: usize = 3;

CONTEXT: The ID generation algorithm starts with short hashes and progressively lengthens them to avoid collisions. The nonce adds randomness at each length. The safety breaks prevent pathological cases from looping forever. These are important algorithm parameters that deserve documentation via naming.

REASONING: If someone needs to debug "why did ID generation take so long?" or "why are my IDs longer than expected?", these named constants immediately point to the tuning knobs.

## Feature: Markdown Rendering

### Purpose
Issue descriptions often contain markdown formatting. Render it properly in Rich mode for better readability.

### File Location
`src/format/markdown.rs`

### CRITICAL: Mode Behavior
Markdown rendering ONLY in Rich mode. Other modes:
- Plain: Strip markdown, output raw text
- JSON: Return raw markdown string unchanged
- Quiet: No output

### rich_rust Markdown Component
```rust
use rich_rust::markdown::Markdown;
use crate::format::OutputContext;

pub fn render_markdown(content: &str, ctx: &OutputContext) -> String {
    if !ctx.is_rich() {
        // Strip markdown for plain/json mode
        return strip_markdown(content);
    }

    let md = Markdown::new(content)
        .with_code_theme("monokai")
        .with_hyperlinks(true)
        .with_width(ctx.width());

    md.render()
}
```

### Supported Elements
- **Bold** and *italic* text
- `inline code`
- Code blocks (with syntax highlighting - see beads_rust-1jcq)
- Lists (ordered and unordered)
- Headers (scale down for embedding)
- Links (clickable in supported terminals)
- Blockquotes
- Horizontal rules

### Integration Points
Markdown rendering used by:
- IssuePanel description section
- Comment bodies
- Any multi-line text fields

